--  Something whose changes take effect only when they are committed
--  (ADR 0026). The command that holds it commits it, as often as it
--  likes; what isn't committed is dropped when the object is released.

interface Transactional is

   procedure Commit;
   --  Make the changes since the last commit take effect. The object
   --  stays open, for more changes. It fails if the changes can't take
   --  effect, and they are then still pending.

   procedure Rollback;
   --  Drop the changes since the last commit.

end Transactional;
